---
// Política de privacidade (GDPR e LGPD). Os [COLCHETES] dependem da entidade
// jurídica (decisão em aberto, ver docs/roadmap.md) e precisam ser preenchidos
// antes de divulgar o site.
import Legal from "../layouts/Legal.astro";
import { SITE, TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY } from "../config.ts";
const email = SITE.contactEmail || "[EMAIL DE CONTATO]";
---

<Legal title="Privacy" description="What happens to the details you leave on the Cap Soleil list.">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="legal__updated">Last updated: 3 October 2026</p>

  <p>
    This notice explains what happens to the details you leave on the list at {SITE.name}. It is written to meet the
    EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and Brazil’s Lei Geral de Proteção de Dados (LGPD).
  </p>

  <h2>Who looks after your data</h2>
  <p>
    <span class="placeholder">[RESPONSÁVEL]</span>, <span class="placeholder">[ENDEREÇO]</span>, is responsible for your
    data (the “controller”). You can reach us at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>When you put your name down:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>your first name and email address;</li>
    <li>your country, if you choose to give it;</li>
    <li>a record of your consent: the version of the text you agreed to, and when;</li>
    <li>how you found us: the campaign tags in the link you followed (for example “instagram”), the website that sent you, and the page you arrived on;</li>
    <li>the kind of device (phone, tablet or computer), the language of your browser, and the hour of the day on the site.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We use no cookies, no analytics and no advertising trackers. We do not store your IP address. To stop abuse, we keep
    a scrambled, one-way code made from your IP address and email for a short time, and delete it within a day.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
  <p>
    To send you Les Lettres du Club: the opening of the Pro Shop and rare news from the club, at most one letter a month.
    We do this on the basis of your consent (GDPR article 6(1)(a); LGPD article 7, I). Keeping the list safe from abuse
    is in our legitimate interest (GDPR article 6(1)(f); LGPD article 7, IX). We do not sell your details or share them
    with anyone for their own use.
  </p>

  <h2>Where it is kept</h2>
  <p>
    Your details are stored by Supabase in the European Union (Paris, France), protected by encryption and access
    controls. Only the club can read the list.
  </p>
  <p>
    This website is delivered by Cloudflare.{TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY && " To tell people from automated programs, the form uses Cloudflare Turnstile, which does not use cookies for tracking."}
    Like any website, these providers briefly handle technical data such as your IP address in order to deliver the page.
    Where a provider is outside the EU or Brazil, it is bound by the safeguards those laws require, such as the European
    Commission’s standard contractual clauses.
  </p>
  <p>We do not send letters yet. Before the first one, we will name the email provider here.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    For as long as you stay on the list. You can leave at any time, and we delete your details within 30 days of being
    asked. If the club stops writing to the list, we delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You may ask to see the details we hold about you, correct them, have them deleted, take a copy, object to their use,
    or withdraw your consent at any time. Withdrawing consent does not affect anything done before.
  </p>
  <p>
    To do any of this, write to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> from the address you signed up with. We will
    reply within 15 days.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you are not happy with our answer, you can complain to your data protection authority: the ANPD in Brazil, or the
    supervisory authority where you live in the EU (in France, the CNIL).
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this notice changes, we will update it here and change the date at the top.</p>
</Legal>
